$ npm run smoke:admin
Run 1: 64 PASS, 2 FAIL. Both were bugs in the smoke script, not on v2:
  - "E deletes the unused cover" HTTP 400 InvalidRequest: the script sent Content-Type: application/json
    with an empty body on DELETE, which Storage refuses. Fixed: the header is sent only with a body.
  - "S deletes the archived recipe" HTTP 204: delete_recipe returns void, so 204 is the right answer;
    the check expected 200. The audit log already showed recipe.delete.
Runs 2 and 3: the two checks above PASS; "E searches USDA" FAIL with HTTP 502 provider_error.
  Measured with a read-only probe (editor account, 8 searches per pass): 7/8, 4/8, 3/8 OK. USDA answered
  the GET form of the search with a non-OK status about half the time, for every query; the same URL with
  the public DEMO_KEY gave HTTP 400 on 5 of 7 calls. Fixed in nutrition-search/contract.ts: the search is
  now POST with a JSON body. After redeploying: 8/8 and 8/8 OK.
